    {
      "id": "claim_fd1c99c3dfb64ba7aed8805bba52b0ea",
      "statement": "The system follows a session-per-handoff model: each handoff (implementation → review → changes-requested) spawns a new agent session for the next profile with a pre-digested current delta rather than the full implementation history, keeping context windows small and token cost flat across review rounds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
